requirements:
Tubes are supplied as specified by the purchaser in one of three conditions:
a) O — Annealed (soft) [supplied in coils or straight lengths];
b) HB — Half-hard [supplied in straight lengths];
c) HD — Hard [supplied in straight lengths].

Tubes are designated by outside diameter and wall thickness, classified across four functional tables:
a) Table W (Micro Bore Annealed): sizes 6, 8, 10 mm OD (thickness 0.6 mm preferred, or 0.8 mm recommended). Max working pressure: 6.2 to 9.0 MPa (preferred) and 8.2 to 14.4 MPa (recommended);
b) Table X (Half-Hard): sizes 6 to 159 mm OD (thickness 0.6 mm to 2.0 mm). Max working pressure: 1.5 to 13.3 MPa;
c) Table Y (Half-Hard and Annealed): sizes 6 to 108 mm OD (thickness 0.8 mm to 2.5 mm). Max working pressure: 2.9 to 18.8 MPa (half-hard) and 2.3 to 14.4 MPa (annealed);
d) Table Z (Hard Drawn): sizes 6 to 159 mm OD (thickness 0.5 mm to 1.5 mm). Max working pressure: 1.5 to 11.3 MPa.

Tubes must satisfy minimum mechanical limits tested in full section or longitudinal strips per IS 1608:
- Annealed (O) [up to 108 mm size]: Tensile strength (Min) = 210 MPa, Elongation (Min) = 40%;
- Half-hard (HB) [up to 159 mm size]: Tensile strength (Min) = 250 MPa, Elongation (Min) = 30%;
- Hard (HD) [up to 54 mm size]: Tensile strength (Min) = 280 MPa;
- Hard (HD) [54 to 159 mm size]: Tensile strength (Min) = 310 MPa.

For tubes designated in Tables W, X, and Y (O and HB tempers), a 45-degree taper drift is plunged into the unannealed tube end per IS 2335. The tube must expand without cracking or showing physical flow:
- Table W (O condition): minimum 30% expansion;
- Table X (HB up to 54 mm): minimum 35% expansion;
- Table X (HB 54 to 108 mm): minimum 25% expansion;
- Table X (HB 108 to 159 mm): minimum 15% expansion;
- Table Y (O condition up to 108 mm): minimum 30% expansion;
- Table Y (HB up to 35 mm): minimum 30% expansion;
- Table Y (HB 35 to 108 mm): minimum 30% expansion;
- Table Z (HD condition): Drift expansion is not applicable.

To ensure reliable leak-proof compression fittings, strict geometric limits are enforced:
- Mean Outside Diameter: half the sum of two diameters measured at right angles;
- Mean Wall Thickness: half the sum of two diametrically opposite wall thicknesses;
- Ovality: calculated as (OD_max - OD_min) / OD_avg;
- Eccentricity: calculated as (WT_max - WT_min) / WT_avg.
